// Title: Terminal Server Client Connection History Cleared - Registry
// Sigma ID: 07bdd2f5-9c58-4f38-aec8-e101bb79ef8d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-10-19 | Modified: 2023-02-08
// ATT&CK: persistence, stealth, defense-impairment, T1070, T1112
// Description: Detects the deletion of registry keys containing the MSTSC connection history
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/windows-server/remote/remove-entries-from-remote-desktop-connection-computer
//   - http://woshub.com/how-to-clear-rdp-connections-history/
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/23/a/vice-society-ransomware-group-targets-manufacturing-companies.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_delete/registry_delete_mstsc_history_cleared.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (ActionType in~ ("RegistryKeyDeleted", "RegistryValueDeleted")) and ((ActionType =~ "DeleteValue" and RegistryKey contains "\\Microsoft\\Terminal Server Client\\Default\\MRU") or ((ActionType in~ ("RegistryKeyDeleted", "RegistryValueDeleted")) and RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Microsoft\\Terminal Server Client\\Servers.*$"))
